[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-5983"] :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}{({x}^{2}+1)}^{3/2},$ $a=1,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{({x}^{2}+1)}^{1/2}\\cdot 2x=2x\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[2x\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=2{x}^{2}+1$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(2{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+x)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(4)^{3}+(4)]-[\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3}+(1)] \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection/ec6224aeb4e8e564738530714605af463186bc5f5294ee76c5b730b1ef83a842" :answer/id #uuid "ce8e4751-073e-50f4-9974-bad132c2770c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{4{x}^{6}+2{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection/adbc8931a91b88991205c508ffcec821817e07e6d865af72f15cc437c1030d9f" :answer/id #uuid "3d4d115a-7ff6-5f6c-86e4-11281d750c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{x}^{12}+{x}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection/f39dfcca7fafb45df183c4f95a393115d0fabcf934a1135834a6f880cf84bb5a" :answer/id #uuid "e71f96ed-ccf8-5505-b53b-25f839de1752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{x}^{7}+{x}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection/9382e5ba5fb7ff594ee5b5ec738d344c6bcebd1036d0a50ef52c4358275cb4e0" :answer/id #uuid "f4efee2d-c776-5837-86fe-fb3bed6fba84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{x}^{8}+2{x}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection/16f6ad6bfb47fc5120f799b7e875c033fdebca51767dd159885c4159491d8321" :answer/id #uuid "e50a56fa-b0ec-5062-8484-87dd0858b0f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{x}^{6}+{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2e0eb18-8712-55ca-9ee8-15ec6d67ba55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15403/selection/f39dfcca7fafb45df183c4f95a393115d0fabcf934a1135834a6f880cf84bb5a" :answer-field/choices ["q-15403/selection/ec6224aeb4e8e564738530714605af463186bc5f5294ee76c5b730b1ef83a842" "q-15403/selection/adbc8931a91b88991205c508ffcec821817e07e6d865af72f15cc437c1030d9f" "q-15403/selection/f39dfcca7fafb45df183c4f95a393115d0fabcf934a1135834a6f880cf84bb5a" "q-15403/selection/9382e5ba5fb7ff594ee5b5ec738d344c6bcebd1036d0a50ef52c4358275cb4e0" "q-15403/selection/16f6ad6bfb47fc5120f799b7e875c033fdebca51767dd159885c4159491d8321"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15403" :question/id #uuid "891e62c5-2f59-5791-9c12-b3816ce7c5d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-15403" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\frac{1}{9}{(2{x}^{3}+1)}^{3/2}$ on $[0,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{9}{(2{x}^{3}+1)}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{3}{2})6{x}^{2}{(2{x}^{3}+1)}^{1/2}={x}^{2}\\sqrt{2{x}^{3}+1}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{2}\\sqrt{2{x}^{3}+1}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{2}\\sqrt{2{x}^{3}+1})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}(2{x}^{3}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+2{x}^{7}+{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{x}^{7}+{x}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection/4d1d264e91a6c03d76b45e91f27b4242e60ae0de8fb6078d6d554c0fc44226ab" :answer/id #uuid "2e6b9962-a78d-520c-a5f1-4696af0045af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection/ba65ff5f1a36a1a453461e562e2628030785b9afa9cf080885d80eeab8ae92f2" :answer/id #uuid "e373f9c7-6b4f-56c1-aa9c-8d907c144ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{1-x}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection/daf0d30ae1945fd38600e1b3bb29cddea4d2d47f113b568a1e8c45457e73f298" :answer/id #uuid "5459e367-7b1c-5808-9d42-ba9227ea2a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection/08ab10542e4fc7e7cda573abe82f87cd0397380fddcf291aceb3faada2ffe4f2" :answer/id #uuid "18433ded-ba7e-52ee-8921-d06888eea8bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection/a0c62776ce4f7407f617cb2777fcd0cf5dce8f9bb2a4b6e1fee5de345b36eb2f" :answer/id #uuid "d80f015c-9f57-57ff-b3b3-76968703a7cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{1+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9f9ce59-0774-5034-a0a7-9893cebb905f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82619/selection/daf0d30ae1945fd38600e1b3bb29cddea4d2d47f113b568a1e8c45457e73f298" :answer-field/choices ["q-82619/selection/4d1d264e91a6c03d76b45e91f27b4242e60ae0de8fb6078d6d554c0fc44226ab" "q-82619/selection/ba65ff5f1a36a1a453461e562e2628030785b9afa9cf080885d80eeab8ae92f2" "q-82619/selection/daf0d30ae1945fd38600e1b3bb29cddea4d2d47f113b568a1e8c45457e73f298" "q-82619/selection/08ab10542e4fc7e7cda573abe82f87cd0397380fddcf291aceb3faada2ffe4f2" "q-82619/selection/a0c62776ce4f7407f617cb2777fcd0cf5dce8f9bb2a4b6e1fee5de345b36eb2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82619" :question/id #uuid "8d968cc2-d41a-56be-9db0-c9b59a5e633c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82619" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{1-x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{1-x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm (-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|)+C \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82619/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82619"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection/35abc8da3c36399825d3d006a9f86486950073f8e06c8f431472ab39a9977779" :answer/id #uuid "b73479c4-84be-5da2-bded-e91dcfd7ee22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{x}^{4}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection/8d77c06b275d1836325d0e097c2cc91c32ad7732bd966ccc3672b4c5adc109d1" :answer/id #uuid "3532d1b2-2f7f-5d4f-834f-9b2ab577e04f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{3}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection/97ff421c39d87ae0509040ebd15896f2c9918c57606da37b894db0ad93da8229" :answer/id #uuid "cd7f4541-a3fd-5656-9251-8a470ff19de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{x}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection/e63511b3de87600c71d12a70e7496c3d7ebc656c1b7f5b708b57136bdb8e4ed0" :answer/id #uuid "c505e7ef-7170-5024-82d9-d10569aca3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{4}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection/81fabe5f32a60f3ea41e27e4b703a0d7d14b7fa7c414b4659a58fec9ce4dd0e4" :answer/id #uuid "971dba84-487b-58a9-b1c1-8e025439e403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{4}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bcee313-9598-5855-8424-1acba228c53f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122389/selection/e63511b3de87600c71d12a70e7496c3d7ebc656c1b7f5b708b57136bdb8e4ed0" :answer-field/choices ["q-122389/selection/35abc8da3c36399825d3d006a9f86486950073f8e06c8f431472ab39a9977779" "q-122389/selection/8d77c06b275d1836325d0e097c2cc91c32ad7732bd966ccc3672b4c5adc109d1" "q-122389/selection/97ff421c39d87ae0509040ebd15896f2c9918c57606da37b894db0ad93da8229" "q-122389/selection/e63511b3de87600c71d12a70e7496c3d7ebc656c1b7f5b708b57136bdb8e4ed0" "q-122389/selection/81fabe5f32a60f3ea41e27e4b703a0d7d14b7fa7c414b4659a58fec9ce4dd0e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122389" :question/id #uuid "64a47477-7e97-505b-9a22-72d4f75d41db" :question/math-academy-id "q-122389" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+400{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+400{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=400{x}^{6}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm 20{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm 20\\int {x}^{3}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm 5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=-5{x}^{4}+2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122389/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122389"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
